+"""Build the M1 n-gram replay set from recorded bonsai traffic (host-only).
+
+Reads the M1 recon inventory
+  bench/results/<date>/m1-ngram/recon/inventory.json
+plus the raw event streams and mem0 SQLite DBs on the host, then writes:
+  bench/.replay/m1/agent.jsonl
+  bench/.replay/m1/mem.jsonl
+  bench/results/<date>/m1-ngram/replay_manifest.json
+
+These replay bodies are the input to the n-gram decode probe (the next item).
+They are deliberately faithful to what the live agent and mem0 actually sent,
+so that decode tok/s on :8089 is measured on the same prompt shapes as the
+recording.  The probe only measures decode speed on the model's reply; it must
+not be run with the memory/agent system prompt (standing fact).
+
+See bench/m1-notes.md for the documented simplifications and the est/recorded
+token-ratio analysis.  All recorded traffic lives on the host only
